        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martinez%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1851, Martinez became the county seat of Contra Costa County, cementing its role as a regional hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://martinezhistory.org/history-of-martinez/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s historic center and waterfront still echo its 19th‑century roots, where early traders and gold‑rush waystations once thrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martinez%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Martinez claims to have birthed the martini cocktail, originally called the “Martinez Special” by a local bartender in 1849.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Martinez"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The John Muir National Historic Site in Martinez preserves the adobe home where the famed naturalist lived and worked in the 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
